`www_chain` seeds the counter (`request_count => scalar @{$next_requests}`, `lib/WWW/Chain.pm:58`), `BUILD` (lines 119-128) does not when the requests come from `start_chain`.

```
package My; use Moo; extends 'WWW::Chain';
sub start_chain { HTTP::Request->new( GET => 'http://x/' ), HTTP::Request->new( GET => 'http://y/' ), 'fin' }
...
My->new->request_count      # 0, with two requests queued
www_chain( $r1, $r2, sub {} )->request_count   # 2
```

Every later step adds its requests (line 112), so the subclass style is permanently short by the first batch.

Done when: `BUILD` sets `request_count` for the `start_chain` path and `t/30-methods.t` asserts `request_count`/`result_count` at the end of the chain.

